                <pb facs="0447" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg365"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/454.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commanding General, Department
                            of Texas, to The Adjutant
                    General.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Antonio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Situation on border much exaggerated in papers. Discreet officers now at El Paso,
                    Del Rio, Eagle Pass, and Laredo have instructions to report by telephone or
                    telegram. There is a decided impression current among people who are conversant
                    with the situation in Mexico that the demonstrations along border are merely to
                    draw attention of Mexican Government away from real points of danger, which they
                    claim will be in the more settled centers of population.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hoyt</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
